# The ComputAItionalThinking ruleset is a separate repository, cloned/installed
# on its own. It is imported by CLAUDE.md, not committed into this repo.
# (no trailing slash: also matches the local symlink form of this path)
/ComputAItionalThinking

# Third-party Lean tutorials cloned locally under tutorials/ (each keeps its own
# .git so it can `git pull` upstream). Not vendored into this repo. To vendor a
# snapshot instead, delete its .git and drop the matching line here.
/tutorials/theorem_proving_in_lean4/
/tutorials/mathematics_in_lean/
/tutorials/logical_verification_2024/

# LeanEuclid — third-party Lean/geometry repo cloned under GeometryPapers/ (its own .git)
/GeometryPapers/LeanEuclid/

# Lean build output (any depth — Mathlib's checkout lives under a nested .lake/)
.lake/
/build/
# Compiled Lean objects (incl. Beeson's Lean 3 .olean artifacts from the zip)
*.olean

# Hook sidecar: every permission prompt this project raises, one line per prompt
# (timestamp, tool, command). Diagnostic state, not project history.
/.claude/permission-requests.log

# Emacs
# backup files
*~
# auto-save files
\#*\#
# lock files (symlink to the editing user)
.\#*
# byte-compiled elisp
*.elc
auto-save-list/
tramp

# macOS
.DS_Store

# The one carve-out: the verbatim Harper PFPL book is Cambridge University Press
# copyright, and its free edition is marked no-redistribution. Keep the raw book
# local; our own OUTLINE.md and generated Lean under HarperBook/ are tracked.
# (Remove these two lines if the repo is private.)
/HarperBook/PFPL.pdf
/HarperBook/PFPL.txt

# redundant self-archive that ships inside the Beeson folder
Beeson/_beeson.zip

# do Carmo, Differential Geometry of Curves and Surfaces — commercial textbook
# (Prentice Hall). Keep the scan local; the freely-posted notes alongside it are tracked.
MathTexts/DifferentialGeometry/doCarmo.pdf
MathTexts/DifferentialGeometry/doCarmo.txt
